# Normalize EOL for all files that Git considers text files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Everything below is byte-exact and must never be touched by EOL normalisation.
#
# The rule above is why these are needed rather than left to Git's own guess:
# `text=auto` applies to every path, and Git's binary detection only looks at the
# first 8000 bytes — a PNG or a DLL that happens to be NUL-free that far in would
# be silently rewritten. For the parity fixtures that would change the pixels the
# golden hashes were taken from; for the extension binaries it would corrupt them
# outright.
*.dll binary
*.lib binary
*.exp binary
*.pdb binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.png binary

# The vendored Open Image Denoise drop is kept byte-identical to the upstream zip, so
# that re-vendoring is a clean diff against the new version rather than a whole-tree EOL
# churn laid on top of the real change. Without this, `* text=auto` above would rewrite
# its headers and licence files on checkout.
addons/image_wrangler/thirdparty/oidn/** -text
